---
import { cardCls, checkCls, crumbCls, emptyCls, rangeCls, selectCls, tabCls, tabsCls, toggleCls } from '../lib/ui';
// Expeditions (was Voyages until 2026-11-07 16:30): the campaigns several ships take part in to find something
// (thorp/fleet.py EXPEDITIONS). #/expeditions lists them, the queue at a glance on top; #/expeditions/<key> is one
// expedition, from one template. #/voyages is still answered.
---
<div class="section" id="voyages">
  <h1>Expeditions <span class="q">campaigns of ships sent to find something: their goals, how they are steered, and what they found</span></h1>
  <nav class={tabsCls('line', 'subnav')} data-orientation="horizontal" data-variant="line" id="vnav">
    <a class={tabCls('')} data-state="active" data-vtab="queue" href="#/expeditions/queue">Queue</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-vtab="expeditions" href="#/expeditions/expeditions">Expeditions</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="vtab" data-vtab="expeditions">
    <div class="cards" id="voyagecards"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="vtab" data-vtab="queue">
    <div class="qswitch" role="tablist" aria-label="how to see the queue">
      <a role="tab" class={toggleCls()} data-state="off" data-qview="glance" href="#/expeditions/queue">At a glance</a><a role="tab" class={toggleCls()} data-state="off" data-qview="every" href="#/expeditions/queue/every">Every voyage</a>
    </div>
    <div class="qview" data-qview="glance">
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="waterspanel">
    <h2>The plan, and the waters each ship sails in <span class="note">the standing queue in its order, as the S2 coordinator sails it: <b>Phaleron</b>, the local waters, is this Mac mini (the Mac lane), <b>foreign waters</b> a GPU hired from Vast.ai (the Vast lane, within the charter's terms); each line about when it sails, for how long, and what it waits for. Times are guides: a voyage at the last like it on this Mac (same corpus and size), a step at its last run, a hold at its longest</span></h2>
    <div id="waters"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the plan…</div></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="overviewpanel">
    <h2>The queue at a glance <span class="note">the voyage at sea, the voyages still to sail and about how many hours that is (each size's mean time), and for every expedition its voyages at sea, queued, finished and failed, and where its next one stands in the queue</span></h2>
    <div id="expoverview"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the queue…</div></div>
  </section>
    </div>
    <div class="qview" data-qview="every">
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="queuepanel">
    <h2>The queue <span class="note">every voyage still to sail, in the order it sails (specs/queue.txt), with its goal: the question its spec asks, or its experiment's where it asks none, and the fitout it was compiled from (its census variation and stage); the voyage at sea first</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll queuescroll"><table id="queuetable" data-nosort><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>ship</th><th title="the SOP version the voyage is built to: its content, tokeniser, parameters, phases and depth">SOP</th><th title="about when it sails: each voyage ahead of it at its size's mean time; ≥ where one ahead has no time yet">sails in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="8" class={emptyCls(true)}>reading the queue…</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section" id="voyage">
  <h1><a class={crumbCls('back')} href="#/expeditions">← expeditions</a> <span id="voyagetitle"></span> <span id="voyagestatus"></span> <span class="q" id="voyagegoal"></span></h1>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="rungover" id="voyageover"></div></section>
  <nav class={tabsCls('line', 'subnav')} data-orientation="horizontal" data-variant="line" id="expnav">
    <a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-etab="overview">Overview</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-etab="at-sea">At sea</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-etab="findings">Findings</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-etab="fleet">Fleet</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-etab="inside">Inside</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="etab" data-etab="overview">
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="voyagelearned"><h2>What it found</h2><p id="voyagelearnedtext"></p>
    <div id="voyagenextwrap" hidden><h2 class="mt">Suggested next steps</h2><ol id="voyagenext" class="nextsteps"></ol></div></section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} data-voyage="table_talk" hidden>
    <h2>The table <span class="note">talk with Table Talk's ships, or any finished ship: type a line and read its answer</span></h2>
    <p><a href="#/expeditions/table_talk/table">Sit at the table →</a></p>
  </section>
  <div class="row">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>What it measures <span class="note">the outcomes the expedition is judged by</span></h2><div class="scroll"><table id="voyageoutcomes"><thead><tr><th>outcome</th><th>metric</th><th>better is</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>The levers <span class="note">what the expedition may change between voyages, and within what limits</span></h2><div class="scroll"><table id="voyagelevers"><thead><tr><th>lever</th><th>range or choices</th><th>about</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
  </div>
  </div>
  <div class="etab" data-etab="at-sea">
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="obspanel">
    <h2>The observation deck <span class="note">this expedition's voyages at sea, read live from their logs: how far each has come and how long it has left, its loss, its speed, the four necessary cards as they stand, and its star chart: each star and trick lit where the voyage found it, numbered in order, to play back. One voyage sails at a time (S2); when none of this expedition's is at sea, where its next one stands in the queue</span></h2>
    <div id="obsdeck"><div class={emptyCls()}>looking out…</div></div>
  </section>
  </div>
  <div class="etab" data-etab="findings">
    <!-- its own instrument, if it has one: data-voyage names the expedition it belongs to -->
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} data-voyage="induction" hidden>
    <h2>The Nevermore over training <span class="note">the trigram engine (frontier books, green) against its random twin (the same libraries and amounts, books chosen at random, grey), two seeds each (seed 1 solid, seed 2 dashed): the Nevermore's natural score at every reading, the mark 0.3 dotted, and the step each voyage first lights it. Success: a 300k lights it on two seeds; repetition did it if the engine lights it and its twin does not (DECISIONS.md, "Discovering the induction head, pre-registered")</span></h2>
    <div class="indverdict" id="indverdict"></div>
    <div class="chart tall" id="indnevermore"></div>
    <div class="row">
      <div><div class="k">Previous-word <span class="s">the head the Nevermore rests on; the mark 0.5</span></div><div class="chart" id="indprev"></div></div>
      <div><div class="k">The copy gain <span class="s">the loss drop from a passage's first copy to its second, nats per token; copying performed at 0.5</span></div><div class="chart" id="indcopy"></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} data-voyage="knockout" hidden>
    <h2>The knockout <span class="note">does silencing a card's heads break chaining in a model that chains? Each card's 8 strongest heads silenced, beside three random draws of 8 heads; a bar per card for the gain lost (cause; the comparator, order), the random draws in grey on the same measure, and each card's rule dotted over it (0.1, and twice its largest random drop), and each card's verdict, necessary or not shown. Outside models only (DECISIONS.md, "The knockout, pre-registered")</span></h2>
    <div id="knockouts"></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} data-voyage="card_census" hidden>
    <h2>The census <span class="note">which of the four necessary cards (previous-word, Nevermore, mover, comparator: the ones every model that chains plays) each size can draw, and its cause-and-effect score, voyage as ablations of the size's own fitout so every variation compares with it. A row per variation (the fitout first), each cell its latest stage's reading (one head or a layer's best two together), green ✓ at the card's mark; cause with its change from the fitout's own. Open a row for its three stages</span></h2>
    <div id="censusgrid"></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} data-voyage="two_facts" hidden>
    <h2>The climb over training <span class="note">each voyage's climb toward chaining two facts at every discovery reading (0 to 5: the rungs performed from the bottom of each chain, plus the next rung's share of its mark, the mean of the four chains), one line per voyage, coloured by size; the dotted levels are the reference ladder; the <a href="#/leaderboard">leaderboard</a> holds each size's best</span></h2>
    <div class="handtools"><select class={selectCls('')} id="voyageclimbwhat"><option value="climb">the climb</option><option value="chaining_lift">the chaining lift</option><option value="logic_gain">the chaining gain (logic deck)</option></select></div>
    <div class="chart tall" id="voyageclimb"></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} data-voyage="book_value" hidden>
    <h2>The fit: what each kind of book is worth <span class="note">the Forgotten Tomes score a pure library of each kind would give, with 90% intervals, lower is better; <b id="fitr2"></b></span></h2>
    <div class="row"><div class="scroll"><table id="fittable"><thead><tr><th>term</th><th>estimate</th><th>90% low</th><th>90% high</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
      <div class="chart" id="fitchart"></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="readingspanel">
    <h2>Its readings <span class="note">every voyage of this expedition on each measure it is judged by (What it measures, on Overview): the latest reading, the best in each column marked</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="voyagereadings" data-nosort><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  </div>
  <div class="etab" data-etab="fleet">
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>The ships <span class="note">each ship this expedition fitted out, its voyages, its mean Forgotten Tomes score, and for each star how many voyages lit it and the soonest step; open one to see it sail</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="voyageruns" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
  <div class="row">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="ftpanel"><h2>The Forgotten Tomes score, voyage by voyage <span class="note">one dot per voyage in the order they sailed, coloured by the expedition's main lever; lower is better</span></h2><div class="chart" id="voyageft"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="lightpanel"><h2>First light <span class="note">each star's score against step: per voyage, the best single head (solid) and the best layer's two strongest heads together (dashed); the dotted line is the threshold, and the moment a line crosses it is first light, lit or lit shared</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools"><select class={selectCls('')} id="voyagestar" title="the star shown"></select></div><div class="chart" id="voyagestars"></div></section>
  </div>
  </div>
  <div class="etab" data-etab="inside">
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="journeypanel">
    <h2>The journey through the layers <span class="note">one voyage read as the data's journey up its stack, bottom to top: the guess the model would make at each depth (bits per byte, and how much each layer lowered it), and out of each half of each layer an arrow sized by how hard it writes into the stream and tilted by which way, up along it, level across it (something new), down against it. Switch on the modules to read each layer's sieves, stars and kink at the step chosen; put a second voyage beside it to compare</span></h2>
    <div class="handtools">
      <select class={selectCls('')} id="journeyA" title="the voyage"></select><label class="note" for="journeyB">beside</label><select class={selectCls('')} id="journeyB" title="a second voyage to compare"><option value="">none</option></select>
      <input class={rangeCls('')} type="range" id="journeystep" min="0" max="0" value="0"><span id="journeylabel" class="note"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="jstages" id="journeystages" hidden></div>
    <div class="handtools" id="journeymods">
      <span class="note">modules</span>
      <label><input class={checkCls('')} type="checkbox" value="push"> push</label><label><input class={checkCls('')} type="checkbox" value="move"> move</label><label><input class={checkCls('')} type="checkbox" value="heading"> heading</label>
      <label><input class={checkCls('')} type="checkbox" value="stars" checked> stars</label><label><input class={checkCls('')} type="checkbox" value="kink" checked> kink</label>
    </div>
    <div class="journeys"><div id="journeyviewA"></div><div id="journeyviewB"></div></div>
  </section>
  </div>
</div>
